  "definition": "Every cell is before -> after. Spikes use the existing analyzer threshold of 20 m/s^2 and its body-minute denominator. Darts count episodes of three-tick displacement greater than 1.4 times a velocity envelope: the maximum reported horizontal speed over six ticks, multiplied by 50 ms, with expected travel at least 3 cm. The six-tick history allows the intentional two-tick snapshot delay while stopping. Contiguous windows are one episode. The earlier integrated-current-velocity proxy is retained separately in darts.json because it can misclassify delayed stopping motion. Discontinuities above 12 m/s are retained separately because the existing analyzer excludes them from speed statistics. Strike-associated dart episodes are counted separately in darts.json; association does not establish whether a dart is intentional. Open/contact snap rates use strafe-minutes. Headless fights do not measure client pose quality.\n",
